# Pairing asks for the daemon address first, then the six-character code.
wait-for Sidekick
expect Pair with your computer
expect Run kobo sidekick init on your computer. It pairs this reader for you.
expect Or type the address it shows
clean
shot sidekick-address
# The field raises the reader's own keyboard, which keeps the steps.
tap-id address.box
wait-for Next
clean
shot sidekick-address-typing
# Back puts the keyboard away and stays on the pairing screen.
tap-id 4294967295
expect-missing Next
expect Or type the address it shows
# Something that cannot be an address is refused under the field.
tap-id address.box
wait-for Next
type bad/host
tap Next
wait-for Enter the address shown on your computer.
expect bad/host
clean
shot sidekick-address-refused
# The field reopens on what was typed, so it is corrected, not retyped.
tap-id address.box
wait-for Next
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
type example
tap Next
wait-for Now the pairing code
expect The six characters shown beside the address.
clean
shot sidekick-code
# A short code is asked for again with what was typed kept.
type abc
tap Pair
wait-for Enter all six characters.
expect abc
clean
shot sidekick-code-short
# Back from the code returns to the address, which gained the default port.
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for Or type the address it shows
expect example:9331
tap-id address.box
wait-for Next
tap Next
wait-for Now the pairing code
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace

# Paired without a network: the splash says so rather than claiming to be
# watching for questions that are going to the terminal instead.
scenario offline
type abc234
tap Pair
wait-for Not connected
expect This reader is not on a network.
expect Change pairing
expect example:9331
expect-missing Watching
clean
shot sidekick-not-connected
# The next poll, ten seconds on, says what went wrong this time.
scenario host-down
wait 10500
wait-for Your computer is not answering.
expect Start kobo sidekick run on it.
clean
shot sidekick-not-answering
scenario network-timeout
wait 10500
wait-for Your computer took too long to answer.
# Change pairing reopens the first step with the old address in the field.
scenario normal
tap Change pairing
wait-for Or type the address it shows
expect example:9331
tap-id address.box
wait-for Next
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
type 127.0.0.1:1
tap Next
wait-for Now the pairing code
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
tap-id kb.backspace
type xyz789
tap Pair
wait-for Paired with
expect 127.0.0.1:1
expect-missing example
# Nothing listens on that port, so the computer is reported as not answering.
wait-for Your computer is not answering.
clean
shot sidekick-repaired
# The pairing survives a restart: no pairing screen, the same address.
restart
wait-for Paired with
expect 127.0.0.1:1
expect-missing Pair with your computer
wait-for Not connected
clean
shot sidekick-after-restart
